{
  "abstract": "We strengthen intermediate moments for exponential sums on the actual perturbed cone $\\omega(k,z)=((k+z)^{3/2}-(k-z)^{3/2})/3$, uniformly over bounded coefficients and rationally translated lattices. Centering local wave-envelope energy and fixing the first two pair frequencies gives exact phase levels on the integer quadric $vk'+dz=H$. We prove positive curvature and derivative bounds for those levels. A local integer-determinant argument retains the third integer coordinate and forces nearby strip points into rational planes. Nonzero product sections, affine sections, both rulings and the exact degenerate directions are all counted. For $K/L$ sufficiently large, the resulting bound is $(DK)^\\varepsilon[(KL)^{q/2}+K^{q-3}L^{q-1}C_\\gamma^{(2q-5)/4}(\\gamma K^2+\\sqrt L)^{(9-2q)/4}]$ for $4<q\\le9/2$, where $C_\\gamma=1+\\gamma K^2/L$. We prove a companion progression bound and retain it where stronger and carry all five monomial branches through the rational-affine and shifted-moment source. At $q=71/16$, the denominator cost is $D^{48/71+\\varepsilon}$ and the cofactor cost is $X^{238/71}$. For every fixed $1517/4837<\\eta\\le33/100$, the lower asymptotic proportion of distinct odd-multiplicity critical-line zeros in $(T,T+T^\\eta]$ is $(\\eta-1517/4837)/8$. Exact algebra and parameter certificates support, but do not independently verify, the analytic proof. Classical determinant, decoupling, component and detector inputs are credited. No effective initial height, simplicity conclusion, or exclusion of an off-line zero is claimed. RH remains unresolved.",
